# Testing Standards for NetGrid

## Test Coverage Requirements
- Aim for 90%+ code coverage across all modules
- Test all public functions and methods
- Cover both success and failure scenarios
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions
- Mock external dependencies consistently

## Test Organization
- Mirror source directory structure in tests/
- Use descriptive test names that explain the scenario
- Group related tests in test classes when appropriate
- Keep individual tests focused on one behavior
- Use fixtures for common test data and setup

## Mocking Strategy
- Mock all system calls (psutil, netifaces, file operations)
- Mock network requests for vendor lookups
- Use pytest-mock for consistent mocking
- Verify mock calls when testing behavior
- Reset mocks between tests to avoid interference

## Test Data
- Use realistic test data that represents real network interfaces
- Create test fixtures for common interface configurations
- Test with various interface types (ethernet, wireless, virtual)
- Include edge cases like missing speed information
- Test with both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses

## Performance Testing
- Test interface discovery performance (< 100ms target)
- Verify table formatting performance (< 50ms target)
- Test memory usage with large numbers of interfaces
- Benchmark vendor lookup caching effectiveness
- Test error handling performance

## Integration Testing
- Test complete CLI workflows end-to-end
- Verify interface filtering works correctly
- Test vendor lookup integration with caching
- Verify table output formatting
- Test error handling in real scenarios

## Test Maintenance
- Keep tests up to date with code changes
- Refactor tests when implementation changes
- Remove obsolete tests promptly
- Use parameterized tests for similar scenarios
- Document complex test scenarios
